  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1961-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The exponents are \\(\\frac{1}{2},\\) \\(\\frac{1}{3},\\) and \\(\\frac{1}{6}.\\) Each term is obtained by multiplying by \\(2^{-\\frac{1}{6}},\\) so the next exponent is \\(\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{6}=0.\\) The fourth term is \\(2^0=1.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Write each radical as a power of \\(2\\)",
        "Check the differences between the successive exponents"
      ],
